\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Great God, indulge my humble  claim;
\par Be Thou my hope, my joy, my rest:
\par The glories that compose Thy name
\par Stand all engaged to make me blest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou Great and Good, Thou Just
\par and Wise,
\par Thou art my Father and my God;
\par And I am Thine, by sacred ties,
\par Thy son, Thy servant bought with blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. With fainting heart and lifted hands,
\par For Thee I long, to Thee I look,
\par As travellers in thirsty lands
\par Pant  for the cooling waterbrook.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With early feet I love to appear
\par Among Thy saints, and seek Thy face;
\par Oft have I seen Thy glory there,
\par And felt the power of sovereign grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Should I from Thee, my God, remove,
\par Life could no lasting bliss afford;
\par My joy, the sense of pardoning love,
\par My guard, the presence of my Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. I'll lift my hands, I'll raise my voice,
\par While I have breath to pray or praise;
\par This work shall make my heart rejoice,
\par And fill the circle of my days.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

